["Nc6",0.12]],"summary":["Objectively sound and tricky in practice for Black: scores 50%, median eval -0.35 around moves 5\u20138.","A steady edge (+1.0) arrives by move 19 in 54% of games; a winning advantage (+6.0) by move 33 in 30%.","Careful with your pawn (28%, 1.3\u00d7 usual) and queen (25%, 1.4\u00d7 usual): the piece you move when the lead slips, usually around moves 19\u201335.","Target their pawn (23%) and bishop (21%, 1.3\u00d7 usual): they give the advantage away with it most often.","Signature shots: sacrifice (1.4\u00d7 typical), zwischenzug (1.2\u00d7 typical).","Wins end by resignation 66%, mate 13%, clock 21% (median move 40)."],"plan":"Usually continues a6 (32%), e5 (30%), g6 (16%). Your pawn is the one to watch (often landing on f6, f4). Aim at their pawn.","tips":["Aim for a steady edge by move 19: 54% of games get there, and 30% reach +6 by move 33.","Watch your queen: it is behind 25% of your lost leads, 1.4\u00d7 the usual rate, landing on e4, e1, g3.","Aim at their bishop: it is behind 21% of their lost leads, 1.3\u00d7 the usual rate, most often the light-squared bishop (60%). The reply wins it outright 20% of the time.","Material changes hands for you on d4 and d5: build pressure there.","They win material on b5 and d5: keep those squares defended.","Look for the sacrifice: it appears 1.4\u00d7 as often as usual in this opening."],"similar":[],"family":"Sicilian Defense"}